<http://data.silknow.org/object/6628417d-521d-3298-b4d9-fb8f752051ae/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "A woman's gown of beige silk, brocaded with large sprays of flowers in shades of green, pink, blue, yellow and brown. The gown is in the English (tight-back) style, open at the front, with elbow-length sleeves and ruched cuffs edged with white silk woven lace (braid).  The bodice and sleeves are lined with linen.  The bodice fronts meet without a stomacher.  The skirts are made of five widths of silk and faced at the hem with blue taffeta.\n\nThe gown was probably made in the 1760s and updated in the early 1780s; sleeve ruffles replaced with gathered cuffs and the robings opened out to meet at the front."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/6628417d-521d-3298-b4d9-fb8f752051ae> .

